From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:13:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wineps.drv: stop putting the PPD's paper size back over the
 stored one.

A printer set to A4 went back to Letter on the next print, every time.

find_printerinfo loaded the stored devmode and then merged the PPD's default
page size into it unconditionally -- the comment said "We'll let the ppd
override the devmode", and it did, including the devmode somebody had already
chosen something in.  The locale-based default that follows only runs when
nothing was stored, so the first run after clearing the settings produced A4
and saved it, and the run after that read A4, overwrote it with the PPD's
Letter, and saved that instead.

The PPD's default belongs to a devmode that has never been touched, which is
what using_default_devmode already says, so ask it first.

Checked with the queue paused: the stored size stays 0x0009 across a print
instead of reverting to 0x0001, and both halves of a manual duplex job now
carry A4 -- the odd one with the automatic tray, the even one with
InputSlot=Manual.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 140c82667b538aea08c96755936af0aed15a0c0a)

diff --git a/dlls/wineps.drv/init.c b/dlls/wineps.drv/init.c
index ad192889527..583368d73e5 100644
--- a/dlls/wineps.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/wineps.drv/init.c
@@ -650,7 +650,11 @@ PRINTERINFO *PSDRV_FindPrinterInfo(LPCWSTR name)
     pi->Devmode = get_devmode( hPrinter, name, &using_default_devmode, size );
     if (!pi->Devmode) goto fail;
 
-    if(pi->ppd->DefaultPageSize) { /* We'll let the ppd override the devmode */
+    /* Only a devmode nobody has chosen anything in takes the PPD's default.
+     * Applying it to a stored one as well undid the choice every time the
+     * printer was opened -- the paper size went back to whatever the PPD says
+     * on the next print, however it had been set. */
+    if(using_default_devmode && pi->ppd->DefaultPageSize) {
         DEVMODEW dm;
         memset(&dm, 0, sizeof(dm));
         dm.dmFields = DM_PAPERSIZE;
